<body><header><div class="wrap"><div class="tag">Minnesota agriculture supply chain</div>
<h1>Should UNFI adjust delivery schedules during severe Minnesota winter weather?</h1>
<p>Weather-based decision support using 2025 observations near Minneapolis–Saint Paul. Explore snowfall, temperature and snow depth to identify periods when delivery plans may need more flexibility.</p></div></header>
<main><section class="card"><h2>Explore the weather data</h2>
<div class="controls"><div><label for="year">Year</label><select id="year"><option value="2025">2025</option></select></div>
<div><label for="month">Month</label><select id="month"><option value="all">All months</option>{month_options}</select></div>
<div><label for="metric">Chart measure</label><select id="metric"><option value="snowfall_in">Daily snowfall (inches)</option><option value="avg_temp_f">Average daily temperature (°F)</option><option value="max_snow_depth_ft">Maximum snow depth (feet)</option><option value="freezing_hours">Hours at or below 32°F</option></select></div></div>
<div class="kpis"><div class="kpi"><div class="value" id="totalSnow">—</div><div class="label">Snowfall in selected period</div></div>
<div class="kpi"><div class="value" id="avgTemp">—</div><div class="label">Average temperature</div></div>
<div class="kpi"><div class="value" id="freezeHours">—</div><div class="label">Hours at or below freezing</div></div>
<div class="kpi"><div class="value" id="peakDepth">—</div><div class="label">Peak snow depth</div></div></div>
<div class="chart-wrap"><canvas id="chart" aria-label="Daily weather measure chart"></canvas></div>
<p class="note" id="chartNote">Each point represents one calendar day. Select a month or measure to update the chart.</p></section>
<section class="card"><h2>What the data suggests for UNFI</h2>
<div class="recommendation"><strong>Recommendation: Yes—use weather-triggered delivery adjustments, rather than changing every winter delivery schedule.</strong>
<p>Keep normal schedules during manageable conditions, but allow earlier dispatch, wider delivery windows, route changes or temporary rescheduling when forecasts indicate heavy snow, accumulating snow cover or prolonged freezing conditions. Prioritize time-sensitive and temperature-sensitive loads, and coordinate changes with suppliers, carriers and receiving locations.</p></div>
<ul><li><strong>Plan ahead:</strong> Review forecasts 24–48 hours before dispatch and flag routes expected to receive significant snowfall.</li>
<li><strong>Protect service:</strong> Build flexible arrival windows and prioritize essential grocery and agricultural inputs when roads are likely to be hazardous.</li>
<li><strong>Control cost:</strong> Avoid blanket early deliveries or unnecessary schedule changes. Compare extra labor, staging and inventory costs with the cost of late deliveries, missed appointments and weather-related disruption.</li>
<li><strong>Measure results:</strong> Track on-time delivery, miles driven, fuel use, carrier wait time, rescheduling costs and product spoilage before and after weather-triggered changes.</li></ul>
<p class="note"><strong>Important limitation:</strong> This file contains weather observations only. It does not include UNFI shipment records, road conditions, carrier rates, fuel costs, delivery delays or crop volumes. It can identify weather risk periods, but cannot prove that schedule changes will reduce transportation costs. Validate the policy against UNFI's actual route and cost data.</p></section>
<section class="card"><h2>Data source and storage (plain-English notes)</h2>
<p><strong>Where the data comes from:</strong> The uploaded CSV was downloaded from Open-Meteo. It contains hourly weather observations for one coordinate near Minneapolis–Saint Paul (latitude 44.956062, longitude -93.20929; elevation 261 m), in the America/Chicago time zone, for January 1 through December 31, 2025. Fields used: time, temperature at 2 metres (°F), snowfall (inches) and snow depth (feet).</p>
<p><strong>Where the data is stored:</strong> Daily summaries are embedded directly inside this HTML file in the JavaScript variable <code>weatherData</code>. The page does not send the data to a server or need a separate CSV file. The uploaded CSV is the original source; this page uses daily summaries calculated from its hourly records.</p>
<p><strong>How the calculations work:</strong> Daily snowfall is the sum of hourly snowfall. Average daily temperature is the mean of hourly temperatures. Maximum snow depth is the largest hourly snow-depth reading that day. Freezing hours counts hourly readings at or below 32°F.</p>
<p><strong>Filter limitation:</strong> The source file covers one location and one year, and has no county or crop field. The year selector therefore contains only 2025; the month selector provides a useful within-year filter. County- or crop-level comparisons require data with those fields or weather data for additional locations.</p>
<p class="source">Source file: open-meteo-44.96N93.21W261m.csv · Data period: 2025 · Units are shown beside each measure.</p></section></main>
<footer>Weather observations are a planning signal, not a road-safety forecast. Check official road and weather advisories before dispatch.</footer>
<script>
// Plain-English data note: these records come from the Open-Meteo CSV uploaded with this project.
// The original file had hourly readings. This HTML stores daily summaries in weatherData below,
// so the page is self-contained and does not need to load a separate CSV or contact a server.
const weatherData={jsondata};
const labels={{snowfall_in:'Daily snowfall (inches)',avg_temp_f:'Average daily temperature (°F)',max_snow_depth_ft:'Maximum snow depth (feet)',freezing_hours:'Hours at or below 32°F'}};
const $=id=>document.getElementById(id);
function selectedRows(){{const y=Number($('year').value),m=$('month').value;return weatherData.filter(d=>d.year===y&&(m==='all'||d.month===Number(m)));}}
function fmt(n,d=1){{return Number(n).toFixed(d);}}
function update(){{const rows=selectedRows(),metric=$('metric').value;
const snow=rows.reduce((s,d)=>s+d.snowfall_in,0),avg=rows.length?rows.reduce((s,d)=>s+d.avg_temp_f,0)/rows.length:0;
const freeze=rows.reduce((s,d)=>s+d.freezing_hours,0),depth=rows.length?Math.max(...rows.map(d=>d.max_snow_depth_ft)):0;
$('totalSnow').textContent=fmt(snow)+' in';$('avgTemp').textContent=fmt(avg)+' °F';$('freezeHours').textContent=freeze.toLocaleString()+' hrs';$('peakDepth').textContent=fmt(depth,3)+' ft';
$('chartNote').textContent=rows.length+' daily observations · '+labels[metric]+'. Select another month or measure to update the chart.';drawChart(rows,metric);}}
function drawChart(rows,metric){{const c=$('chart'),r=c.getBoundingClientRect(),dpr=window.devicePixelRatio||1;c.width=Math.max(1,Math.floor(r.width*dpr));c.height=Math.max(1,Math.floor(r.height*dpr));
const ctx=c.getContext('2d');ctx.scale(dpr,dpr);const W=r.width,H=r.height,L=58,R=18,T=20,B=42,pw=W-L-R,ph=H-T-B;ctx.clearRect(0,0,W,H);if(!rows.length)return;
const vals=rows.map(d=>d[metric]);let min=Math.min(0,...vals),max=Math.max(...vals);if(metric==='avg_temp_f'){{min=Math.floor(Math.min(...vals)/10)*10;max=Math.ceil(Math.max(...vals)/10)*10;}}if(max===min)max=min+1;
const y=v=>T+(max-v)/(max-min)*ph,x=i=>L+(rows.length===1?pw/2:i/(rows.length-1)*pw);
ctx.font='11px Arial';ctx.strokeStyle='#e2e9ee';ctx.fillStyle='#5d6b78';ctx.lineWidth=1;
for(let j=0;j<=4;j++){{const v=min+(max-min)*j/4,yy=y(v);ctx.beginPath();ctx.moveTo(L,yy);ctx.lineTo(W-R,yy);ctx.stroke();ctx.textAlign='right';ctx.fillText(v.toFixed(metric==='freezing_hours'?0:1),L-9,yy+4);}}
ctx.strokeStyle='#28658a';ctx.lineWidth=2;ctx.beginPath();rows.forEach((d,i)=>{{if(i===0)ctx.moveTo(x(i),y(d[metric]));else ctx.lineTo(x(i),y(d[metric]));}});ctx.stroke();
ctx.fillStyle='#28658a';rows.forEach((d,i)=>{{if(rows.length<=100||i%Math.ceil(rows.length/80)===0){{ctx.beginPath();ctx.arc(x(i),y(d[metric]),2.5,0,Math.PI*2);ctx.fill();}}}});
ctx.fillStyle='#5d6b78';ctx.textAlign='center';const step=Math.max(1,Math.ceil(rows.length/8));for(let i=0;i<rows.length;i+=step)ctx.fillText(rows[i].date.slice(5),x(i),H-15);if(rows.length>1&&(rows.length-1)%step!==0)ctx.fillText(rows[rows.length-1].date.slice(5),x(rows.length-1),H-15);
}}
$('year').addEventListener('change',update);$('month').addEventListener('change',update);$('metric').addEventListener('change',update);window.addEventListener('resize',update);update();
</script></body></html>'''
out="/mnt/data/unfi_minnesota_winter_delivery_analysis.html"
with open(out,"w",encoding="utf-8") as f:f.write(html)
